WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:37.250
Serve the old version. Visitors use the existing version while the next release is prepared. Establish user-visible metrics and rollback conditions before shifting traffic.

2
00:00:37.250 --> 00:01:11.750
Start the replacement. Create new capacity without immediately removing all old instances. Download, initialization and dependency setup take time and need spare resources.

3
00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:58.083
Check readiness. The readiness gate verifies the instance can serve the intended request. A running process with missing dependencies should not receive normal traffic yet.

4
00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:35.833
Shift traffic gradually. Send a bounded share to the new version and drain old work deliberately. Monitor errors and latency for real user operations, not only process health.

5
00:02:35.833 --> 00:03:08.167
Keep data compatible. Both versions can access the database during rollout. Expand and migrate safely before removing fields or behavior the old version still needs.

6
00:03:08.167 --> 00:03:52.417
Validate rollback. Stop or reverse traffic movement if the release violates its criteria. Code rollback cannot magically reverse incompatible or destructive data changes.
